<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagriamel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1960s–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nagriamel is a political and customary movement founded on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/espiritu-santo">Espiritu Santo</a> in the New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> in the mid-1960s by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-stevens">Jimmy Stevens</a> and Chief Paul Buluk. It demanded the return of uncultivated land claimed by European planters and defended customary ways of life. Backed by some French settlers and American business interests, it opposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuaaku-pati">Vanua'aku Pati</a> and led the failed secession of Espiritu Santo in 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagriamel.jpg" alt="Nagriamel" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vectorized by Froztbyte · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Vemerana.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
